Vault secret management (per-service):
- HashiCorp Vault deployed in vault namespace (dev mode, auto-unsealed).
- Root token never committed — injected via scripts/bootstrap-vault-secret.sh using stdin-to-kubectl pattern.
- Vault setup Job (one-shot) enables KV v2 at secret/, Kubernetes auth method, per-service policies (secret/data/devops-platform/<svc> read-only), per-service Vault roles bound to <svc>-sa ServiceAccounts with 1h TTL.
- Apps reference VAULT_TOKEN from vault-root-token Secret with optional: false (fail-closed).
- Apps have /livez (process check) vs /readyz (Vault-reachable check) split probes.
- Each app has dedicated ServiceAccount (users-service-sa, products-service-sa, orders-service-sa).
- NetworkPolicy default-deny + allow-list: app→Vault:8200, app→DNS:53, app→postgres:5432, Prometheus scrape ingress, intra-namespace.
