5. Orchestration Scripts & CI/CD
No root-level Makefile or docker-compose. Orchestration is layered:
Scripts (scripts/):
- bootstrap-vault-secret.sh: Creates/rotates vault-root-token Secret out-of-band. Generates random 64-char hex token if VAULT_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN unset. Pipes via stdin to avoid ps/disk exposure. Requires namespace pre-exists.
- validate-security.sh: 4 checks — (1) Gitleaks full-history scan, (2) Trivy CRITICAL/HIGH scan on :latest images, (3) Vault initialized+unsealed via jq parsing, (4) Real Vault token authentication via vault token lookup in one-off pod. --ci mode fails on missing tools. Exits 1 on any failure.
CI/CD (.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml — 370 lines):
- Triggers: push to main/develop (with path filters on app/, k8s/, terraform/, ansible/, .github/, scripts/, .gitleaks.toml), PR, workflow_dispatch, nightly cron.
- Concurrency: cancel-in-progress per ref.
- Permissions: contents: read default, escalated per job.
- Jobs (sequential where needed):
